diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c5080df..bdc33ea 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,6 +16,52 @@ Make sure that `flash-attention` and `DeepSpeed` are installed.
 2. Replace `*.py`, `added_tokens.json`, `config.json`, `special_tokens_map.json`, `tokenizer_config.json` in the base model folder with the files in the[ChatTS-8B](https://huggingface.co/bytedance-research/ChatTS-8B) or [ChatTS-14B](https://huggingface.co/bytedance-research/ChatTS-14B) repo according to type of your base model.
 3. **Initialization:** To ensure training stability, we strongly recommend using Xavier normal initialization for the parameters of `ts_encoder`. You can first load the model created in the previous steps using `AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained` in Python, then apply Xavier normal initialization to the `model.ts_encoder` part, and finally save the model using `save_pretrained`. For detailed API usage, please refer to the [official Transformers documentation](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/en/index).
 
+## Optional: replace the MLP encoder with TimesFM 2.5
+
+ChatTS can keep its existing processor, `<ts>...<ts/>` merge logic, datasets, and LLM while using
+[`google/timesfm-2.5-200m-pytorch`](https://huggingface.co/google/timesfm-2.5-200m-pytorch)
+as a frozen time-series feature extractor. The adapter returns the same `(features, patch_cnt)` interface as the
+native encoder:
+
+```text
+ChatTS [value, mask] input
+  -> TimesFM 2.5 patching (32 points / token)
+  -> frozen 20-layer TimesFM backbone (1280-d)
+  -> trainable 2-layer TS-to-text projector
+  -> unchanged ChatTS token merge and LLM
+```
+
+Install the optional dependency:
+
+```bash
+# TimesFM 2.5 requires Python >= 3.10.
+pip install -e ".[timesfm,deepspeed]"
+hf download google/timesfm-2.5-200m-pytorch model.safetensors config.json
+```
+
+Then add the following options to a normal ChatTS training command:
+
+```bash
+--ts_encoder_type timesfm2_5 \
+--timesfm_model_name_or_path google/timesfm-2.5-200m-pytorch \
+--timeseries_sft_lr 1e-4
+```
+
+Runnable templates are provided in
+[`scripts/full/train_timesfm2_5_stage1.sh`](scripts/full/train_timesfm2_5_stage1.sh) and
+[`scripts/full/train_timesfm2_5_stage2.sh`](scripts/full/train_timesfm2_5_stage2.sh).
+
+Important behavior:
+
+- TimesFM stays frozen; only the projector and the parameters selected by the normal fine-tuning mode are optimized.
+- TimesFM uses 32-point patches instead of ChatTS' original 8-point patches, reducing time-series tokens by about 4x.
+- TimesFM weights remain an external dependency and are not copied into every ChatTS checkpoint.
+- Stage-1 checkpoints record `ts_encoder_type=timesfm2_5`; stage 2 can use `--ts_encoder_type auto`.
+- The current adapter accepts at most 16,384 points per individual series.
+- The old MLP encoder weights are not reusable: train the new projector in stage 1 before stage-2 SFT.
+- Load trained checkpoints through this patched LLaMA-Factory loader; a plain upstream
+  `AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(...)` does not know how to reconstruct the external TimesFM adapter.
+
 
 ## Steps to reproduce
 1. Download the training datasets from [ChatTS-Training-Dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/ChatTSRepo/ChatTS-Training-Dataset). Put the folders under `data/` (e.g., `data/align_256/`, `data/align_random/`, etc).
